From: Vincent Donnefort <vdonnefort@google.com>
Date: Wed Mar 5 17:04:23 2025 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: KVM: arm64: Fix THPs reclaim with ballooning

A ppage content can't be read without either that ppage out of the
pinned_page tree or without the mmu_lock taken. Fix potential race
between vCPUS to decrease ppage->pins and free the page.

Also the memory accounting was wrong. Once the huge-page is freed, we
need to account for that entire size.

Bug: 278749606
Bug: 278011447
Bug: 400307522
Fixes: e602818486b6 ("ANDROID: KVM: arm64: Huge page support for pkvm_pinned_page")
Change-Id: I1a9f29ce9e63d707f59129aafd78e3d1d858614f
Signed-off-by: Vincent Donnefort <vdonnefort@google.com>

Origin: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common 63a99c1fb8e57d859ec3f51d49f4d74fbf84f3b8
Batch: B-2 (P4 kvm/pKVM cluster) - Class A, apply as-is; predicted ABI delta zero

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/pkvm.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/pkvm.c
index e04bb2f..1b93341 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/pkvm.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/pkvm.c
@@ -539,6 +539,7 @@ void pkvm_host_reclaim_page(struct kvm *host_kvm, phys_addr_t ipa)
 	struct mm_struct *mm = current->mm;
 	struct kvm_pinned_page *ppage;
 	unsigned long index = ipa;
+	u16 pins;
 
 	write_lock(&host_kvm->mmu_lock);
 	ppage = mt_find(&host_kvm->arch.pkvm.pinned_pages, &index,
@@ -549,16 +550,16 @@ void pkvm_host_reclaim_page(struct kvm *host_kvm, phys_addr_t ipa)
 		else
 			WARN_ON(1);
 
-		if (!ppage->pins)
+		pins = ppage->pins;
+		if (!pins)
 			mtree_erase(&host_kvm->arch.pkvm.pinned_pages, ipa);
 	}
 	write_unlock(&host_kvm->mmu_lock);
 
-	WARN_ON(!ppage);
-	if (!ppage || ppage->pins)
+	if (WARN_ON(!ppage) || pins)
 		return;
 
-	account_locked_vm(mm, 1, false);
+	account_locked_vm(mm, 1 << ppage->order, false);
 	unpin_user_pages_dirty_lock(&ppage->page, 1, host_kvm->arch.pkvm.enabled);
 	kfree(ppage);
 }
